# Email notifications

Larger-scale **blockframes** for TEC emails to local authorities (and the respondent, for N244). Frames use readable draft copy; **From** and **To** stay as grey address bars (no real email addresses). Hover those bars for the element name.

Reuse the email shell (`partials/blockframe/email`) when adding further notification types.

## Overview

| Email | Audience | Timing | Case links |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| In-time and out-of-time applications | Local authority | One batch per night | Case list only (filter by state) |
| Out-of-time decision — CO rejection | Local authority | When CO and LA disagree | Direct link to the case |
| Out-of-time decision — CO agreement | Local authority | Included in nightly batch | Same as nightly summary |
| N244 filed by respondent | Local authority | Individual | Direct link to the case |
| N244 filed by LA | Respondent | Individual | Direct link to the case |

## Nightly batch: in-time and out-of-time applications

One overnight email per local authority. **Summary counts only** — how many in-time and out-of-time applications were received. Includes a link to the case list so the authority can find cases by matching case state (`revoked` or `awaiting_OOT_decision`). No direct links to the cases named in the summary.

Where the court officer and the local authority **agree** an out-of-time decision, that outcome is covered by this same nightly summary (no separate agreement email).

